WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.5 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Institutional funding

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Check your readiness before you write an institutional proposal.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Check registration, audited accounts, policies and MEAL first.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Profile funders: priorities, eligibility, cycle and route.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Start as a consortium partner if you are not ready.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: yearly state audit in place; next is a government handloom scheme covering 50% of a dye unit. Application due February.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write your readiness check and two funder profiles.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
